WEBVTT

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:44.910
America emerged victorious from the spring World Baseball Cup after a fierce, sixteen-inning game.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:49.340
The World Cup players who played for the pride of our nation

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:53.920
have been greeted by the passionate cheers of fans as they returned to their Major League training camps.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.510
Can I have a word on that last hit at the World Cup?

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:07.600
I just see that grand slam as the first step into my new baseball career.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.610
With the season starting soon,

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:10.860
are you confident in your skills?

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:15.610
I aim and rise only toward higher levels.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.910
What's Gibson's current status as a pitcher?

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.560
Will he be retiring?

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.950
His surgery was a success, but it will be a long time before he's fully recovered.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:31.000
I don't think we'll see him back on the mound.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.240
This retirement is happening right before the start of the season.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:37.500
Isn't this quite a loss for the team?

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.290
Yes, it is.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:45.220
However, he has had an amazing career in the Majors.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.240
At the moment, I can only thank him for making so many dreams come true.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:57.710
The World Cup has left us with quite a bit of drama, including the sudden retirement of pitcher Joe Gibson.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:04.330
However, many people are wondering whether that game truly determined who is the best in the world.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:12.080
There are many players who didn't play for national teams in order to train for the MLB season.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.750
Now that they've been set loose, what sort of games will we see?

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.830
The Major League season is right around the corner.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.430
Hey, Watts!

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.530
Show us some great games again this year!

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.500
Thank you!

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:34.850
Show us what you've got, Mr. Hornets!

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:38.060
Mr. Watts.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.490
You seem to be as popular as ever.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.760
Could you comment on how the Hornets plan to respond to their fans' hope

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.530
that they'll win the championship after twenty-five years?

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.640
I'm a closer,

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:53.150
so I like us to have a big lead so I don't have to pitch.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.040
However,

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.190
I personally think we have a great chance this year.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:59.710
After all, we have some lively newcomers this year.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:04.490
Are you referring to Mr. Keane, who'll be the starting catcher this year?

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:07.680
Or are you referring to leadoff hitter Mr. Roy, who's made himself quite a home as shortstop?

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.360
Or could you be referring to <i>him</i>?

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:11.930
Who knows?

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:14.770
I'll leave that up to your imagination.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.170
To the Hornets training camp, please.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.910
Hey, Keane!

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.550
You're practicing hard, as always.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.690
I heard the super rookie's coming back today.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:45.410
Yeah.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.660
That's what I've heard.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.500
You two were friends in the minors, right?

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.180
Well, do you think you can take my pitches once you've warmed up with him?

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:59.770
Rosario looks pumped to take on the rookie.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.390
Nelson, Parker.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:06.450
He must be a pretty good rookie to make our ace that serious.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:10.690
For the sake of our team, I sure hope he lives up to his name.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:20.470
When will you be pitching next?

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.130
I saw the World Cup.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:27.800
You'll show off your amazing pitching in MLB next, right?

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.600
I'm looking forward to it.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:51.620
Super Rookie

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:51.620
Super Rookie

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:55.160
Hey, we've been waiting for you, Mr. Shigeno!

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:59.330
I saw your wonderful pitching at the World Cup.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.120
Oh, thanks.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:10.130
Embarrassingly enough, I didn't know you played for our AAA Bats until my staff told me.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.890
Boss, who is this old man?

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.260
Y-You idiot!

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.390
He's the owner!

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.680
He's the owner of Indiana Hornets, Mr. Larry Lance.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.940
That's all right.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:29.150
Anyway, we're quite blessed to have someone like you working with us.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:37.240
Your promotion to the Majors is pretty much set in stone after the World Cup results,

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:40.190
but we'll need to have you pitch a few exhibition games.

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.380
You seem to have rested well in Japan,

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:46.970
so you'll be ready in four days for our game against the New York Titans, right?

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:47.880
Yeah.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:52.340
We have Watts as the closer, so you'll probably be pitching early,

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.890
but I'm sure you'll do fine with your stamina.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:56.730
We expect great things from you.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.520
Do your best, Mr. Shigeno.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.110
Sure.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:08.780
Shigeno, huh?

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.270
A true gem.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:15.690
He can draw in the crowds with his performance, and we'll also gain a Japanese fan base.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.340
Use him as much as possible right away.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.420
Got it?

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:22.070
But Owner,

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:25.470
it's his first Major League season.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:27.910
We shouldn't be reckless and have him crumble under the pressure.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.130
Hey, now, Mr. Stacy.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:34.390
Isn't your coaching contract up for renewal this year?

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:39.100
Don't you need to show results, no matter how you do it?

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:53.950
Shigeno!

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:54.470
Shigeno!

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:55.930
Good luck!

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.440
Mr. Shigeno!

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:00.510
Do you have a moment?

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:02.670
May I have a few words with you?

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:06.280
I'd like to ask you about the World Cup and your plans for the future.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:07.670
Yes, I'd like a few words as well.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.780
I'm Tomita from Sunrise Sports.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.030
I'm Morita from Weekly Major.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.720
May I interview you after practice?

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.320
I'd love to hear your comments about the—

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:16.850
Shut up!

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:18.210
Interviews?

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:20.600
I have nothing to say about a game I lost!

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.530
Don't you have a sense of delivery?

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:25.650
No interviews! Goodbye!

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:29.730
Boy is he wild...

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.590
Though it's not like we didn't know that he hates interviews.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.380
What did he mean by "delivery"?

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:37.100
He probably mistook it for "delicacy."

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.120
Damn them.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:41.200
Making a fool out of me.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:41.920
What the hell's their...

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.670
Hey, you're back.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:47.780
Oh, you two!

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:50.910
Who are you again?

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.730
We're Roy and Danston!

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:55.650
We've been together since the Bats days.

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:57.390
Sorry about that.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:01.560
Well, I've gotta say, you put on quite a show at the World Cup.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.480
That face-off with Gibson Jr. gave me the shivers.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:09.970
I heard the owner even came to personally welcome you.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:11.900
Your success in the Majors is pretty much guaranteed.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.200
You guys too?

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:16.860
Shut up!

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.200
All of you!

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.660
H-Hey, what's wrong with you?

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.780
Nothing, damn it!

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:29.570
What the hell...

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:33.550
I can't stand how everyone treats me here.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.100
I performed well?

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:37.090
I pitched well?

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.750
You must be kidding!

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.640
Why isn't anyone yelling at me?!

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.310
They got a homer out of me!

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.250
I'm a losing pitcher!

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.850
Hey, losing pitcher!

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.270
Wh-What was that?!

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.180
Sanders!

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:53.820
Yo!

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:55.700
What a surprise!

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:56.870
You're here, old man?

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.860
I didn't see you in first half of the camp.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.530
If you're still on the roster at this time of the year,

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.540
you'll definitely be selected for the MLB—

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.550
No!

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.790
I'm not a player anymore.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.290
I see...

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:17.400
You re-injured yourself when you were training in the off-season...

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:18.350
Yeah.

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:23.060
I'm just a bullpen catcher and personnel for the Hornets.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.680
It's a fun job, actually.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:30.440
I get paid to do something related to baseball, and I get to watch MLB games all the time.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.920
Living the dream, right?

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:35.900
In any event,

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.440
good job at the World Cup.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:42.490
It's a shame that you lost in the end,

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:44.490
but you pitched pretty well against America.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:47.410
It was commendable pitching.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:49.780
Not that again.

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:52.460
I've had enough pity already.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.960
Hey, what are you so grumpy about?

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.010
I'm not showing you pity.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:58.370
I'm just telling the truth.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:59.630
The truth?

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.170
Wanna know the truth?!

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:03.180
The truth is that I lost!

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:07.220
My record 103 mph pitch was hit for a walk-off grand slam!

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:13.100
Pitching against Gibson at the World Cup,

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:16.590
I lost my one and only predestined match!

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.320
<b>Honda Family</b>

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:20.650
And for a little while, I even considered quitting baseball.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:25.250
But...

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:27.770
baseball is all I have.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.150
Upon realizing that fact,

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:32.790
I came back here, mustering every ounce of conviction in me to start over again!

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:36.380
I don't want anyone showing me pity!

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:39.720
I see.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:44.140
Then let me tell you a thing or two, you incompetent pitcher.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:47.660
You considered quitting baseball?

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:49.230
Give me a break!

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:53.810
You've barely stepped into the Majors, so don't act like some veteran!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.990
Your record 103 mph pitch?

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:58.350
Shut up!

00:11:58.350 --> 00:11:59.990
If he hit your 103 mph,

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.950
then pitch at 105 or even 200 mph, you dumbass!

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:06.360
You think that's impossible?

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:08.030
I sure as hell don't.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:13.330
Everyone is excited about the potential of a nineteen-year-old youngster like you.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:17.750
It's time to stop looking behind yourself.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:22.420
You're not wearing the Japanese national uniform anymore.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:26.820
Lead the Hornets to victory on this grand MLB stage!

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.270
You bet.

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.330
Play ball!

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.320
All right, play ball!

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.670
Not bad.

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:00.230
He's in great condition.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:01.200
Yeah.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:04.220
It seems he's still got the energy from the World Cup.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:08.680
Ow...

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.540
My hand hurts.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:14.730
He must've gotten better in the World Cup.

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:18.630
Oh, you're here, Keane.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.690
Can you take Shigeno's pitches for a bit?

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:23.920
Sure.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.160
Thank you.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:34.860
Shigeno's pitches are much sharper than they used to be.

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:39.790
The lower pitches will make your mitt turn a bit, so be careful catching those, Keane.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.430
Oh, sorry.

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:45.940
What am I saying? I'm just a bullpen catcher.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:51.260
He never changes...

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:53.660
That stupid seaweed-head needs to show some respect!

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.480
What a nice sound.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:05.860
How is it?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:08.270
Feels good catching it, doesn't it?

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:12.000
He didn't challenge the American team with nothing.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.150
We'll see about that.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:18.580
No matter how well he pitches in the bullpen, I can't trust those throws.

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:23.740
The masses seem to be praising him quite a bit,

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:28.180
but all he did was strike out some batters who weren't prepared to play early spring games.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:31.570
Not to mention he lost six points in a critical situation.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.220
I don't call that good pitching.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:36.550
Over-evaluating players only puts them on a high horse.

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:38.960
Wh-What was that?!

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:40.350
Who's on a high horse?!

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:41.760
Hey, stop, Shigeno.

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:43.460
Actually, this is great.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:45.580
He's talking smack about you.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:48.320
I didn't like his tone, damn it!

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:52.310
Well, we'll see what you can do against the Titans in four days.

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:57.290
MLB isn't anything like those amateur World Cup games.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:02.200
Well, try not to crush the owner's hopes.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:05.990
Sorry to make you wait, Rosario.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:10.050
W-Well, he's not really talking smack about you.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:14.890
He's just motivating you to prepare for the MLB season.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.690
What was that?!

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.650
Are you saying Shigeno's performance was just a fluke?!

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.690
I didn't say that.

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:34.950
I'm just saying that we can't evaluate his real strength when all he did

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.080
was pitch against a temporary team made of off-season players.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.500
He doesn't know how scary MLB is yet.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:44.270
Now that I think about it, he pretended that he was injured

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:47.930
and stayed in the minors when he got promoted to MLB last year, right?

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:50.140
He was probably just scared.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:51.150
Are you kidding me?!

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:52.590
He was just thinking about the Bats and—

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:53.930
That's enough, Roy.

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:58.820
No matter what you say, he's gotta prove his strength on the baseball mound.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:00.920
That's how MLB works.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.000
I get it.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.230
No matter how much people talk about me,

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:12.240
these guys don't see me as their teammate yet.

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.380
Bring it on.

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:18.080
There'd be no point in being in MLB without a challenge like this.

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:23.270
First and foremost, I'll shut down the prominent Titans lineup

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:25.530
and prove my strength to these guys.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:48.680
The Hornets are using Shigeno as their starting pitcher.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:52.120
Do you think he's fully recovered from the walk-off grand slam?

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:54.770
Yeah, I talked to him before the game.

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:55.910
He looked pretty pumped.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:58.850
He's probably fine, with that thick head of his.

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.390
The quota for now is six innings.

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:05.790
Pitch between 100 and 110 pitches, and don't take more than three points.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.730
If you don't manage your stamina well, you won't last.

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:11.760
I know that!

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:17.010
Now hitting: number 8, Cabela.

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:26.140
Well, let's see how he does.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.100
Play ball!

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:38.410
Strike out!

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:41.700
All right.

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:44.390
He's pitching well from the start.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:46.920
Strike!

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:50.220
He pitches to almost exactly where the mitt is.

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:52.250
I insulted him the other day,

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:56.420
but his ball control and speed really have improved.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:09.260
Strike!

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:13.520
His fork isn't bad either.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:17.230
It started losing its spin near the end of the America game,

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:19.740
but it should be effective if he only makes around 100 pitches.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.960
His pitching at the World Cup wasn't a fluke.

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:27.310
He undoubtedly has what it takes to pitch in MLB!

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:30.040
Strike out!

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:41.140
Now hitting: number 13, Alex.{onscr}

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:48.020
Looks like he's completely recovered.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:55.360
Foul!

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.190
You're not bad.

00:19:01.190 --> 00:19:03.360
I like pitchers like you.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:06.940
Looks like I'll have...

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:10.010
plenty of fun from now on!

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.290
Strike out!

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:18.300
All right! Three up, three down!

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.300
Nice going, Shigeno!

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:25.640
Victory's in your hands!

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:34.580
You're pitching well, rookie.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.080
Nice pitching.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.900
Guess you're up next.

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:43.650
I hope you'll show me how real MLB players do it,

00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:49.040
since I'm just a youngster who's in way over his head, right, veterans?

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:53.500
Y-You...

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:54.750
Cocky little...

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.860
You're doing great, Junior.

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:22.560
Yeah.

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:28.260
Thanks to the World Cup, my peak came a little early, when I should've been saving it for the season.

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:30.410
Shigeno was the starting pitcher.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:35.400
He attracted quite a bit of attention to see how he'd do against the Titans' lineup of sluggers,

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:40.580
and he finished six innings and two outs, giving up only three hits, three walks, and no runs,

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:43.750
taking a victory with a near-perfect performance.

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:44.760
Oh, is that him?

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:48.590
If we're lucky, we might play him in an interleague game.

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:52.450
Well, see you later.

00:20:56.470 --> 00:20:58.510
You've begun to run forward again.

00:20:58.510 --> 00:21:00.380
That's why you're my rival.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.510
I don't care about some interleague game.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:07.900
I'll send your pitch to the stands in the World Series,

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:10.910
playing for the highest title in Major League Baseball.

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:15.330
And this time, my bat won't break.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:24.300
With just three days until opening day, this game will be the last exhibition game for both teams,

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:27.000
as the Hornets play against the Grizzlies.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:31.850
For the starting pitcher, the Hornets have brought out the attention-drawing rookie, Goro Shigeno!

00:21:32.570 --> 00:21:36.850
He pitched against the Titans in his previous game and didn't give up a single run, pitching 100 mph left and right.

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:40.660
He'll undoubtedly make the opening season roster.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:44.920
Now, what sort of pitching will he show us today?

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:03.560
You're finally a Major Leaguer.

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:05.990
Goro, congratulations.

00:22:07.690 --> 00:22:09.270
I also need to do my best.

00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:13.060
It's decided.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:17.140
Your MLB debut will be the third game of the season,

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:21.270
playing at home against the Seattle Seagulls.

00:22:23.190 --> 00:22:29.610
You're fifth on the pitching rotation, but the owner wanted your first game to be at home.

00:22:30.230 --> 00:22:31.250
Can you do it?

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:33.330
You bet.

00:22:34.190 --> 00:22:36.880
I'll give a flashy debut.

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:59.230
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:59.230
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:04.610
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:04.610
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:10.860
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:10.860
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:15.620
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:15.620
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:22.290
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:22.290
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:28.130
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:28.130
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.930
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.930
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:39.390
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:39.390
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:45.860
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:45.860
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:51.110
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:54.570
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:51.110 --> 00:23:54.570
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:57.040
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.570 --> 00:24:03.420
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:57.040 --> 00:24:03.420
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:07.250
sotta

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:07.250
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:15.430
Preview

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:15.430
Preview

00:24:10.680 --> 00:24:13.610
At last, I'm standing on the MLB mound.

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:15.400
What was that?

00:24:15.400 --> 00:24:18.740
I could pitch a no-hitter for my debut game?!

00:24:19.180 --> 00:24:20.640
Interesting.

00:24:20.640 --> 00:24:22.460
All right, I'll do it!

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:25.100
Next time on Major: A Prominent Debut!

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:30.030
Next Time

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:30.010
Next Time

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:29.960
A Prominent Debut!

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:30.010
A Prominent Debut!

00:24:25.740 --> 00:24:30.640
Run toward the stage of your dreams!
